INT. SHARK TANK TUNNEL, MARINE AQUARIUM - NIGHT

Blue gloom. Sharks glide overhead. The tunnel's acrylic arch glows.

A MAN IN OVERALLS crouches at a maintenance panel, drill whining. A WOMAN IN A DIVE SUIT, TAMSIN VOLK, swims past outside the glass, signalling. The third, a LOOKOUT in a guard uniform, DESHAWN, leans on the rail, watching the corridor.

MAN IN OVERALLS
Panel's open.

TAMSIN (O.S.)
(through earpiece)
Clock's running. Two minutes.

DESHAWN
Quiet. Footsteps.

A torch beam sweeps the far wall. All three freeze. A hammerhead drifts across the glass.

MAN IN OVERALLS
Seal's cut. Pearl case is behind it.

TAMSIN (O.S.)
Don't touch the alarm bar.

TEODORO
(whispering)
I never touch the bar.

DESHAWN
Teodoro, hurry.

TEODORO
Got it.
